# The ONNX operators and types Kitten mini v0.8 uses, which are the only kernels
# compiled into OpenChime's minimal ONNX Runtime (scripts/build_onnxruntime.sh,
# ARCH-111). Generated by ONNX Runtime's create_reduced_build_config.py
# --format ORT --enable_type_reduction from the model as converted on BOTH
# architectures (scripts/build_kitten.sh), because the conversions differ: on
# arm64 ONNX Runtime has half-precision kernels and keeps MatMul and Add in
# MLFloat16, where on amd64 it casts them to float. Regenerate it from both when
# the model changes (docs/READ-ALOUD.md §4). A kernel missing here makes the model
# fail to load, loudly, rather than run wrong.
